WEBVTT

00:07.716 --> 00:10.552
One minute to go.

00:10.635 --> 00:14.389
Well then, Ms. Utahime Iori,

00:14.472 --> 00:17.892
please give us a touching
and encouraging speech.

00:17.976 --> 00:18.810
What?

00:18.893 --> 00:21.563
Well…

00:21.646 --> 00:23.189
Well…

00:23.273 --> 00:26.401
Although injuries are inevitable…

00:26.484 --> 00:28.737
Well…

00:28.820 --> 00:30.613
Just help each other from time to time.

00:30.697 --> 00:32.073
Something like that?

00:32.157 --> 00:33.575
Time's up.

00:33.658 --> 00:36.578
Gojo, you…

00:36.661 --> 00:39.956
With that,
the Sister-School Goodwill Event…

00:40.498 --> 00:43.626
begins!

00:43.710 --> 00:45.545
Show some respect to your seniors!

00:46.212 --> 00:47.172
Was that Ichiro?

00:47.255 --> 00:48.715
Idiot.

00:49.382 --> 00:50.884
Where's Todo?

00:50.967 --> 00:53.762
Why do you assume I would know?

00:53.845 --> 00:55.472
Let's get along well.

01:04.898 --> 01:06.983
Where could the Cursed Spirits' boss be?

01:07.650 --> 01:10.570
I think it will be placed
in the middle of both teams.

01:10.653 --> 01:12.822
But it probably won't stay still.

01:13.406 --> 01:16.076
When the time comes,
divide into Panda team and Megumi team

01:16.159 --> 01:17.994
since they are good at finding enemies.

01:18.745 --> 01:20.997
We'll leave the rest to you, Yuji.

01:21.081 --> 01:22.373
Got it!

01:26.669 --> 01:29.798
Where are you going?

01:31.299 --> 01:32.383
That's a small fry.

01:37.013 --> 01:38.640
Stop, Maki!

01:46.397 --> 01:49.818
All right! Seems like everyone's here.

01:49.901 --> 01:52.320
Come at me together!

01:57.033 --> 01:58.201
Split up!

02:01.913 --> 02:03.623
Todo's alone.

02:04.249 --> 02:06.584
It was the right choice to change to Yuji.

02:11.089 --> 02:13.508
I already knew this, but he's a monster.

02:13.591 --> 02:16.010
Yes. So ignore them.

03:58.738 --> 04:00.949
BEFORE THE TEAM BATTLE

04:01.032 --> 04:04.994
Todo will definitely rush to defeat us.

04:05.078 --> 04:08.831
Mai might also follow him
to come after me.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.543
Todo is a monster.

04:12.627 --> 04:17.715
In the worst-case scenario,
everyone will be wiped out.

04:19.300 --> 04:25.431
Originally, I planned to leave Panda
or Megumi to hold him. But now…

04:26.849 --> 04:29.519
Itadori, this task will be yours.

04:29.602 --> 04:30.478
What?

04:31.312 --> 04:34.232
I don't want to remove people
who can find the enemy.

04:35.108 --> 04:39.320
You don't have to beat him.
Just hold him back for a while.

04:39.404 --> 04:41.406
But you need to be bold.

04:41.489 --> 04:44.200
To put it bluntly, you're unexpected help,

04:44.284 --> 04:46.411
so it won't affect us
if you have to retire.

04:46.494 --> 04:47.662
That's too much!

04:48.413 --> 04:50.123
I'm sorry, Megumi.

04:50.206 --> 04:52.542
You wanted to fight Todo, didn't you?

04:53.376 --> 04:55.420
No, I don't mind it.

04:55.503 --> 04:57.005
You're so calm.

04:58.798 --> 05:01.384
But, Panda, since I'm fighting him…

05:01.467 --> 05:02.635
-What?
-What?

05:03.511 --> 05:05.471
I'll win.

05:09.434 --> 05:11.144
Your speed is quite good.

05:11.728 --> 05:14.689
Are you serious?
I hit pretty hard just now.

05:21.654 --> 05:23.239
Payback time, first-year student.

05:23.323 --> 05:24.907
Try your best to defend!

05:42.759 --> 05:44.343
My hand's still intact, right?

05:45.720 --> 05:47.680
I thought it flew off.

05:47.764 --> 05:51.434
If the Cursed Spirit wasn't there,
I would've been in big trouble.

06:24.425 --> 06:25.802
Over already?

06:33.184 --> 06:35.853
All right. Who's next?

06:41.859 --> 06:43.611
Are you serious?

06:51.035 --> 06:54.872
You keep punching my head.

06:54.956 --> 06:57.792
What if I become dumber?

06:58.751 --> 07:00.378
Don't worry.

07:00.461 --> 07:05.383
Takada said,
"It's better for a boy to be stupid."

07:05.466 --> 07:07.051
Who's that?

07:07.135 --> 07:09.387
I'm not interested in idols.

07:09.470 --> 07:12.056
Then why do you know she's an idol?

07:12.140 --> 07:14.100
You know her, don't you?

07:14.725 --> 07:17.145
What's your name, first-year?

07:17.228 --> 07:18.646
Yuji Itadori.

07:18.729 --> 07:21.107
I see. Yuji Itadori.

07:21.190 --> 07:23.651
I have a question for you.

07:25.445 --> 07:27.655
What type of woman do you like?

07:28.531 --> 07:29.740
What?

07:30.241 --> 07:32.160
What type of woman?

07:32.243 --> 07:34.662
Why are you asking this now?

07:34.745 --> 07:38.166
Don't mind me.
It's just my way of evaluating people.

07:40.626 --> 07:44.672
I don't understand,
but if I had to choose…

07:48.426 --> 07:52.763
A girl with big head
and big butt, perhaps?

07:52.847 --> 07:55.099
Someone like Jennifer Lawrence.

07:57.727 --> 07:59.645
What?

08:05.902 --> 08:09.822
SHOUNEN WEEKLY MAGAZINE

08:10.531 --> 08:12.909
The new series is quite interesting.

08:12.992 --> 08:13.826
Really?

08:16.537 --> 08:17.663
-What?
-What?

08:30.635 --> 08:32.553
I'm going to confess to Takada.

08:33.137 --> 08:34.889
What? Don't do that!

08:34.972 --> 08:38.267
I don't want to comfort you.
It's troublesome.

08:38.351 --> 08:40.978
Why are you sure that I would get dumped?

08:43.481 --> 08:46.984
On the other hand,
why do you think she would agree?

08:47.068 --> 08:50.696
Anne Sullivan once said this
to Helen Keller.

08:51.197 --> 08:55.201
"How can a fool think about losing
before he does it?"

08:55.284 --> 08:57.036
That's what Inoki said.

08:58.538 --> 09:00.206
I'm sorry.

09:00.289 --> 09:02.500
I already have someone I like.

09:20.560 --> 09:23.145
Is it possible
that I'm that someone she likes?

09:23.729 --> 09:25.439
How could it be possible?

09:28.609 --> 09:30.403
Come on. Let's go.

09:32.863 --> 09:34.949
I'll buy you ramen.

09:50.881 --> 09:54.343
"At home, we are invincible…"

09:56.345 --> 10:00.766
Looks like we're best friends.

10:00.850 --> 10:02.852
Even though you just asked for my name?

10:04.645 --> 10:06.689
Just go straight.

10:06.772 --> 10:08.274
But Todo is there.

10:08.357 --> 10:12.236
It's okay. He's the one who said
we can do as we please.

10:20.494 --> 10:22.955
New Shadow Style, Simple Domain!

10:25.416 --> 10:26.417
Batto Sword Drawing!

10:31.839 --> 10:33.507
His response is quick!

10:33.591 --> 10:35.092
Although I hesitated,

10:35.176 --> 10:37.511
my attack didn't scratch him at all!

10:43.142 --> 10:44.810
I'm surrounded.

10:45.519 --> 10:48.814
What? These guys…

10:48.898 --> 10:50.316
Aren't they…

10:54.111 --> 10:55.780
trying to kill me?

11:01.452 --> 11:02.703
This technique…

11:02.787 --> 11:03.704
What?

11:03.788 --> 11:06.207
I swapped positions with Itadori!

11:07.875 --> 11:08.876
Hey.

11:10.169 --> 11:12.129
I told you, didn't I?

11:12.213 --> 11:14.465
I'll kill you if you get in my way.

11:15.091 --> 11:16.550
No.

11:16.634 --> 11:19.470
You said, "I'll kill you if you order me."

11:19.553 --> 11:21.347
Was that Itadori?

11:21.430 --> 11:24.600
No, was that Todo's cursed technique?

11:24.683 --> 11:27.311
It's all the same. Leave!

11:34.777 --> 11:36.070
Retreating?

11:36.153 --> 11:37.154
Lame.

11:37.655 --> 11:39.115
I'm so glad!

11:39.615 --> 11:41.909
You must kill him.

11:41.992 --> 11:44.578
That depends on Itadori.

11:44.662 --> 11:46.414
Don't order me around.

11:46.497 --> 11:48.290
What's wrong with these guys?

11:48.374 --> 11:50.918
They want to kill me,
yet they're infighting.

11:52.711 --> 11:55.840
After all,
I'm not the kind of tasteless man

11:55.923 --> 11:58.134
who shows mercy to his best friend!

12:04.515 --> 12:05.641
Oh, man.

12:06.225 --> 12:08.394
That's why I said stay out of it.

12:09.061 --> 12:10.813
What a bad start.

12:11.647 --> 12:13.983
Since I'm in charge
of hunting Cursed Spirits,

12:14.066 --> 12:16.152
I need to find them from the air first.

12:18.279 --> 12:20.698
This is so troublesome.

12:21.282 --> 12:24.076
I'm going to work hard.
I'm cute today, as usual.

12:24.160 --> 12:25.369
Knock her down.

12:27.455 --> 12:28.789
Oh, no!

12:30.458 --> 12:33.544
Mai and Mechamaru, go help Nishimiya.

12:33.627 --> 12:37.214
-Understood.
-Okay, we need her anyway.

12:49.018 --> 12:50.186
Kamo.

12:50.895 --> 12:54.482
Are you guys planning to kill Itadori?

13:02.615 --> 13:03.532
Something is wrong.

13:03.616 --> 13:05.284
Something is weird.

13:05.367 --> 13:08.037
Kyoto team is moving as a whole.

13:08.704 --> 13:11.207
They are around the area
we separated from Yuji.

13:11.290 --> 13:13.626
Isn't everyone from Kyoto team there?

13:14.627 --> 13:16.962
Is the target there?

13:17.463 --> 13:18.422
No.

13:18.506 --> 13:20.799
Unless the Grade 2 Cursed Spirit
is cunning,

13:20.883 --> 13:22.510
the Divine Dog will detect it.

13:24.303 --> 13:28.307
Are they trying to kill Itadori?

13:28.390 --> 13:30.809
What's this? This is absurd.

13:35.231 --> 13:36.815
It's possible.

13:37.399 --> 13:38.317
Kelp.

13:38.901 --> 13:42.321
It's that I didn't feel hostility
from them,

13:42.905 --> 13:46.325
but that was before Yuji's
survival surprise.

13:48.369 --> 13:52.331
It's possible if that was
Principal Gakuganji's instruction.

13:52.414 --> 13:58.337
Is Kyoto team a group of cowards
who will obey orders to kill people?

13:58.420 --> 14:00.631
Our perceptions are different.

14:00.714 --> 14:04.343
You lived with Yuji before.

14:04.426 --> 14:08.055
We only just knew that he's a good guy.

14:08.138 --> 14:10.975
He's cheerful,
and that's rare among Jujutsu Sorcerers.

14:11.058 --> 14:12.351
However,

14:13.143 --> 14:15.854
for those who don't know Yuji,

14:15.938 --> 14:20.359
Sukuna's vessel is a scary existence.

14:21.110 --> 14:24.738
It's similar to exorcising curses.

14:25.281 --> 14:30.369
It's easy for Jujutsu Sorcerers
to cross the line in the first place.

14:33.956 --> 14:35.708
Megumi, let's go back.

14:36.458 --> 14:37.668
I'm sorry.

14:37.751 --> 14:39.795
What are you apologizing for?

14:40.379 --> 14:42.339
If our comrade dies,

14:42.423 --> 14:44.842
what's the point
of winning the Goodwill Event?

14:46.343 --> 14:50.472
Nobara and I will go confirm
Yuji's safety.

14:51.056 --> 14:52.766
He's not answering his phone.

14:52.850 --> 14:56.270
Toge will carry on to hunt Cursed Spirits.

14:56.854 --> 14:57.938
Bonito flakes.

14:58.022 --> 15:00.900
I know you're worried about Yuji too.

15:01.483 --> 15:04.153
But if my guess is right,

15:04.236 --> 15:10.409
they're trying to assassinate Yuji
in the chaos of team battle.

15:10.492 --> 15:14.079
There won't be any assassination
if the team battle ends.

15:14.163 --> 15:15.456
I see.

15:15.539 --> 15:16.415
Salmon.

15:16.498 --> 15:18.083
I'm worried about Maki, too.

15:18.584 --> 15:22.046
We can't let them kill Yuji,
and we'll win the team battle.

15:22.546 --> 15:23.923
Of course.

15:28.427 --> 15:31.013
Answer the call once it rings, Fushiguro!

15:32.014 --> 15:36.894
Speaking of which, why didn't the school
provide a radio or Bluetooth headset?

15:37.478 --> 15:39.104
I don't want it.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.941
It's distracting
and I'll be shocked when it rings.

15:42.024 --> 15:44.401
Just take it off during the battle!

15:49.365 --> 15:50.824
That hurt.

15:52.952 --> 15:55.537
So that's Fushiguro's Nue…

15:56.038 --> 15:57.873
The wings are electrified.

15:57.957 --> 16:00.834
It will affect my movements temporarily.

16:03.212 --> 16:08.008
-Nishimiya!
-Nishimiya!

16:08.592 --> 16:11.512
-Let's play.
-Let's play.

16:11.595 --> 16:14.765
So uncultivated and not cute.

16:15.432 --> 16:19.228
Kamo, are you guys trying to kill Itadori?

16:19.812 --> 16:23.232
What if I say yes?

16:23.315 --> 16:25.317
You failed.

16:25.401 --> 16:28.737
Itadori won't be killed so easily.

16:33.158 --> 16:34.660
We have no reason to kill him.

16:35.411 --> 16:36.578
There is a reason.

16:36.662 --> 16:39.456
At least, the higher-ups
and the Big Three Sorcerer Family do.

17:11.697 --> 17:13.741
What great endurance.

17:13.824 --> 17:16.493
He also takes advantage
of the terrain actively!

17:18.162 --> 17:19.621
He's gone.

17:22.708 --> 17:25.169
He also follows up
with the next attack quickly.

17:32.217 --> 17:34.595
The best part is…

17:37.014 --> 17:39.641
this amazing power!

17:39.725 --> 17:42.478
This tiny body has stronger power than me.

17:42.561 --> 17:45.647
So he can cause a blow
with a small amount of cursed energy.

17:46.148 --> 17:50.569
So it's difficult to predict his actions
from the cursed energy flow!

17:50.652 --> 17:54.114
However, this delayed cursed energy…

17:54.198 --> 17:57.159
Only this…

17:58.494 --> 18:01.789
It's wrong!

18:01.872 --> 18:08.504
It's wrong!

18:14.301 --> 18:16.220
Was that Todo?

18:16.762 --> 18:18.097
I guess so.

18:18.180 --> 18:23.268
I vaguely understand
why you can't get rid of Yuji.

18:24.269 --> 18:27.564
So why did you separate from Noritoshi?

18:27.648 --> 18:30.692
Are you hiding your cursed techniques
from your own people?

18:35.322 --> 18:37.950
I'm sorry about Itadori.

18:38.450 --> 18:42.204
It may sound like an excuse,
but I'm not like the others.

18:42.287 --> 18:47.292
However, I don't intend
to let you guys win the Goodwill Event.

18:47.793 --> 18:48.919
RECOMMENDATION

18:49.002 --> 18:52.714
You know a Jujutsu Sorcerer's promotion
depends on recommendations, right?

18:53.298 --> 18:55.384
Even Jujutsu Sorcerers
with no direct contact

18:55.467 --> 18:58.053
will know about the Goodwill Event.

18:58.804 --> 19:00.973
Students who stand out
in the Goodwill Event

19:01.056 --> 19:04.726
have a higher chance for promotion
during the schooling period.

19:05.936 --> 19:10.065
By the way, you can't recommend
your own students.

19:10.566 --> 19:15.237
For example, Mr. Gojo
can't recommend Itadori to Grade 1.

19:15.904 --> 19:20.242
I want to be independent
as soon as possible and earn a living.

19:24.830 --> 19:25.831
Why?

19:28.750 --> 19:29.960
Because I'm poor.

19:30.043 --> 19:31.753
And I have two younger brothers!

19:31.837 --> 19:33.672
Are you okay?

19:33.755 --> 19:35.799
Are you getting along with Mai?

19:35.883 --> 19:37.426
Aren't you being too nice?

19:37.509 --> 19:38.385
What?

19:38.886 --> 19:40.220
I guess.

19:41.430 --> 19:43.599
I won't go easy on you.

19:44.933 --> 19:46.310
No problem.

19:46.393 --> 19:49.104
I'm not saying this
to make you show mercy.

19:51.690 --> 19:53.066
My friend.

19:53.150 --> 19:57.988
That delayed cursed energy
is your bad habit!

19:58.071 --> 19:59.615
You mean the Divergent Fist?

20:00.616 --> 20:02.993
What's with this guy?

20:04.453 --> 20:08.373
You can never beat me
so long as you're satisfied with this.

20:09.208 --> 20:15.380
We're no longer best friends
if you're satisfied with this level.

20:15.464 --> 20:17.299
Are you fine with that?

20:17.382 --> 20:20.385
What should I do? I'm okay with that.

20:20.469 --> 20:23.513
-Are you fine staying this weak?
-What?

20:27.059 --> 20:28.602
I'm not.

20:30.312 --> 20:31.939
Right?

20:32.606 --> 20:35.901
My best friend!

22:06.783 --> 22:08.410
-Juju Stroll!
-Juju Stroll!

22:08.493 --> 22:12.664
QUESTION
WHAT KIND OF PERSON DO YOU LIKE?

22:13.415 --> 22:16.501
Someone that's at least stronger than me.

22:17.002 --> 22:18.170
What?

22:18.670 --> 22:21.173
Why should I tell you?

22:21.757 --> 22:24.968
I hate guys that are good-for-nothings,
poor, stinky, petty, and dead.

22:25.927 --> 22:28.764
Do you know Sebastian Stan?

22:30.348 --> 22:32.100
He has a great body.

22:32.184 --> 22:38.023
Well, it's normal to like handsome guys.

22:38.899 --> 22:41.818
I mean it's fun to be
with someone like him.

22:41.902 --> 22:45.447
But more importantly,
he has to make me feel that

22:45.530 --> 22:48.575
he's the only one for me!

22:49.701 --> 22:50.535
What?

22:50.619 --> 22:53.663
Oh, my! You're making me embarrassed!

22:54.206 --> 22:55.540
Well…

22:55.624 --> 22:58.126
You see, well…

22:58.210 --> 22:59.753
What was it again?

23:00.545 --> 23:01.880
Well…

23:01.963 --> 23:03.381
You know…

23:03.465 --> 23:05.467
That one who looks nice.

23:05.550 --> 23:08.095
The one with the unique bangs. Come on.

23:08.178 --> 23:09.429
You know, right?

23:11.056 --> 23:14.392
Someone who looks nice…

23:31.326 --> 23:33.036
Oh, Miwa?

23:33.120 --> 23:34.621
That's right!
